## 1. REST controller: POST create owner

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain3/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

The `addOwner` method (lines 100-113) plus the `isDuplicateOwner` helper it depends on (lines 215-223):

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    if (isDuplicateOwner(owner)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}

// ...

private boolean isDuplicateOwner(Owner owner) {
    return this.clinicService.findOwnerByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .anyMatch(existing ->
            Objects.equals(existing.getFirstName(), owner.getFirstName())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getLastName(), owner.getLastName())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getAddress(), owner.getAddress())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getCity(), owner.getCity())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone()));
}
```

Notes:
- The controller implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface (from OpenAPI). Request body type is `OwnerFieldsDto`; response is `OwnerDto`. Bean Validation on the incoming DTO produces a 400 via the advice (see section 5).
- 409 CONFLICT is returned when an identical owner (same firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) already exists.
- There is also a V2 controller at `.../rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`, but it only exposes a paged `listOwnersPage` GET — no create.

## 2. Owner entity/model

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain3/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person`. Fields:
- `address` — `@NotEmpty`
- `city` — `@NotEmpty`
- `telephone` — `@NotEmpty @Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10) @Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")`
- `pets` — `@OneToMany(cascade = ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = EAGER) Set<Pet>`

Standard getters/setters for address, city, telephone.

`lastName` (and `firstName`) live on the superclass `Person`:
File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain3/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`
- `firstName` — `@Column(name = "first_name") @NotEmpty`
- `lastName` — `@Column(name = "last_name") @NotEmpty`

Note: `telephone` has both `@Digits(integer = 10)` and a strict `@Pattern` requiring exactly 10 digits. `lastName` only requires `@NotEmpty` (no length/format constraint).

